Relevant columns and their potential usage
• `reference_name`: filter to chromosome 1 (`'chr1'`).  
• `start_position`, `end_position`: restrict rows to the genomic window 55 039 447‑55 064 852 (inclusive / half‑open) and later compute region length.  
• `alternate_bases`: ARRAY that keeps one STRUCT per alternate allele.  
    – `alternate_bases.alt`: actual alternate base; just for inspection.  
    – `alternate_bases.AC`: alternate‑allele count (per allele, already QC‑filtered).  
    – `alternate_bases.AN` does not exist (AN is at the row level), so `alternate_bases.AC_raw` could be consulted when raw counts are needed.  
    – `alternate_bases.vep`: ARRAY of VEP annotations for that allele.  
        * `alternate_bases.vep.SYMBOL`: gene symbol, used to list distinct genes that harbour variants in the window.  
• `AN`: total number of alleles (2 × number of chromosomes that passed QC) for every variant row.  
• All other columns are not absolutely required for the requested summary but may be useful for exploratory checks.

Conditions that will be reused
```
reference_name = 'chr1'
AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
```

Ten progressively more complex example queries
(they all rely on the only table that is allowed:  
`bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`).

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at the first 20 variants in the region of interest
SELECT
  reference_name,
  start_position,
  end_position,
  reference_bases,
  alternate_bases
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect the first alternate allele and its allele count (AC)
SELECT
  start_position,
  ab.alt    AS alt_base,
  ab.AC     AS allele_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show per‑variant total number of callable alleles (AN) and
--                the sum of AC across all alternate alleles
SELECT
  start_position,
  AN,
  SUM(ab.AC) AS total_AC_per_variant
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
GROUP BY start_position, AN
ORDER BY start_position
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List distinct gene symbols (via VEP) touched by the window
SELECT DISTINCT
  v.SYMBOL AS gene_symbol
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab,
     UNNEST(ab.vep) AS v
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND v.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count the number of variants (rows) in the region
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS n_variants
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Aggregate total AC (all alternate alleles summed) in the window
SELECT
  SUM(ab.AC) AS total_allele_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Aggregate total AN (diploid allele number) across all variants
SELECT
  SUM(AN) AS total_number_of_alleles
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Combine counts: number of variants, total AC, total AN
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT start_position)                           AS n_variants,
  SUM(ab.AC)                                               AS total_AC,
  SUM(DISTINCT AN)                                         AS total_AN
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
     UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab
WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Produce list of gene symbols with number of variants per gene
SELECT
  v.SYMBOL                        AS gene_symbol,
  COUNT(DISTINCT g.start_position) AS n_variants_in_gene
FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1` AS g,
     UNNEST(g.alternate_bases) AS ab,
     UNNEST(ab.vep) AS v
WHERE g.reference_name = 'chr1'
  AND g.start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  AND v.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY gene_symbol
ORDER BY n_variants_in_gene DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final one‑stop summary – number of variants, summed AC, summed AN,
--                 distinct gene symbols, and mutation density (bp per variant)
WITH region AS (
  SELECT 55064852 - 55039447 + 1 AS region_length -- inclusive bp span
),
variants AS (
  SELECT
    start_position,
    AN,
    SUM(ab.AC) AS variant_AC
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
       UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab
  WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
    AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
  GROUP BY start_position, AN
),
gene_list AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    v.SYMBOL AS gene_symbol
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.gnomAD.v3_genomes__chr1`,
       UNNEST(alternate_bases) AS ab,
       UNNEST(ab.vep) AS v
  WHERE reference_name = 'chr1'
    AND start_position BETWEEN 55039447 AND 55064852
    AND v.SYMBOL IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  r.region_length,
  COUNT(*)                          AS n_variants,
  SUM(variant_AC)                   AS total_allele_count,
  SUM(AN)                           AS total_number_of_alleles,
  r.region_length / COUNT(*)        AS bp_per_variant_density,
  ARRAY_AGG(DISTINCT gene_symbol)   AS distinct_gene_symbols
FROM variants, region AS r, gene_list
GROUP BY r.region_length
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is self‑contained and explores a different angle, incrementally leading to a complete summary of genetic variation within the specified chromosome‑1 window in gnomAD v3 genomes.
